A foundation model needs the sampling rate of its input, as it already needed the channel names: `FrozenBackboneTransformer` and `FoundationClassifier` (and the `FoundationEmbeddingModelConfig` and `NeuralFineTuneConfig` that build them) raise an error without `sfreq`. Without it, the input was taken to be at the model's own rate, so data at any other rate went to the model unresampled and on the wrong time scale, with no warning. The examples in the foundation-model docs now pass `sfreq` and `ch_names`.
